# ENCODING-SAFE OUTPUT (UTF-8 Protection)

PROBLEM: German umlauts get corrupted when pasted as plain text (GÃ¼nter, bezÃ¼glich, etc.).
SOLUTION: Output customer replies in markdown code blocks to preserve UTF-8 encoding.

## RULE:

When outputting a customer reply **in chat** (section 6 of RE), DO NOT paste it as plain text.

INSTEAD: Wrap it in a markdown code block:

```
Guten Tag Silvana Spajzer,

vielen Dank, dass Sie uns bezüglich der
Hardware-Rückforderung...
[rest of reply]
```

The triple backticks preserve UTF-8 encoding and prevent mojibake corruption.

